                ],
                "fontFamily": "Inter",
                "text": "Flutter's showLicensePage is a master-detail route: an app bar, a back chevron, list tiles, a second page per package. The rail is always on screen, so a back chevron is a second navigation surface, and a row that pushes a page loses the list it came from. So the notices are drawn like every other list here \u2014 rows that open IN PLACE, one at a time, in the panel the per-track routing dialog already uses. A long document is still a list. Both LEGAL rows on SYSTEM \/ about reach it: there is one page, and they are two ways of asking for it."
              }
